 "**THE CHAIN AS THE CHAIR NOW RECOMMENDS IT (each outward step waits for the owner's word in session):** RUN 24 green → the cheap CI-only pre-runs at the gate (npm audit; the hostile-locale eight; `deno task check:edge` + `test:edge`; a targeted `saves.js` coverage lower bound) → close PR #48 → push the ledger → push the consist (hook honest) → PR with a REFRESHED body (seven stale statements listed in the report; the materially wrong one says 'migration 201 after merge') → watch the branch's CI → ⛔ THE OWNER'S HAND: `supabase login` / `link` / `db push` (201–203) / `migration list` (the CLI is not installed on this box; production credentials are never typed by the chair) → the owner hands over the live head NUMBER → the chair runs `SUPABASE_MIGRATION_HEAD=203 npm run validate:migration-head` and commits `supabase/applied-head.json` = 203 with its verification text on the branch → merge on green → the Vercel build proceeds (or the owner clicks Redeploy on the merge commit if neither deploy secret is set) → ⛔ THE OWNER'S HAND: redeploy the EIGHT edge functions whose shared bundles moved (`generate-narrative`, `custom-content`, `interpret-session`, `surveyor-autonomy`, `construct-realm`, `construct-settlement`, `surveyor-byok`, `ai-analyst`) FROM A CLEAN CHECKOUT OF THE MERGE COMMIT (never the stale main checkout) and `npm run ops:post-deploy` with production credentials. "
 "**WHAT THE OWNER MUST HEAR BEFORE THE MERGE (put in the chair's report):** the purchases lock (`src/lib/launchGate.js`, `VITE_PURCHASES_OPEN`) does NOT exist on master — this merge is what first obeys the 09-16 order; the data-loss cure stops new loss, heals NO save already damaged, and a client ROLLBACK after it re-opens the defect (one committed tick re-erases whoever the cure protected) — rollback is destructive, not neutral; nine signed shift records mean a seed generated on production today will not reproduce byte-identically after the deploy (each shift owner-worded; the aggregate stated here for the first time); world locks are REMOVED (a coup in a save that had locked its incumbent now falls without an approval queue) — existing saves behave differently; anonymous visitors are narrowed (no thorp; no pre-generation options); a new persisted browser key `anonDraft` keeps an anonymous visitor's dossier across a refresh; migration 201 widens the AI entitlement to staff incl. the provider-key write door; Edit Mode is dark because the editor does not exist yet (all sixteen architected modules absent) — two forward hazards slotted for EM-D0 / EM-C4a: `TIER_GATE.premium.editMode` must be CREATED, and the architected state key `editMode` COLLIDES by name with the shipped dossier boolean. "
